    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d858">

                <pb facs="0895" n="887" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C112/1317: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-29T11:00:00+01:00">January 29, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 29—6:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1090. My 1089, October 6, 10 a.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d858-f1"/> In view of the
                    fact that many states including some of the chief military powers have still not
                    defined their attitude to the principle of a convention on publicity for
                    national defense expenditure the Council yesterday unanimously decided to
                    postpone fixing the date for a new meeting of the Bureau until the next ordinary
                    session of the Council.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d858-f1" n="2" xml:id="d858-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram No. 1086, September 17, 1937, 2 p.m., from the Consul
                    at Geneva, and footnote 45, <ref target="frus1937v01#pg_23"><hi
